      "writtenOn": "2022-11-30T17:42:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The SoC has a single DP-capable port. On the board only one port is muxed to this DP-capable port, which happens when the EC receives the HPD high VDO, and the EC reconstructs the analog HPD waveform to signal the SoC. The kernel driver listens the analog HPD signal and doesn\u0027t know which port is muxed. So this USB mux state doesn\u0027t matter.",
